  "id": "collaborative-empiricism",
  "term": "collaborative empiricism",
  "definition": "Collaborative empiricism is a way of working in cognitive behavioural therapy in which therapist and patient work together during structured sessions to examine and solve problems. It emphasizes a shared, joint approach between both people in therapy.",
